import{_ as t,o as a,c as s,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"One workspace and the Graph","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/graph-episode.md","filePath":"records/graph-episode.md"}'),n={name:"records/graph-episode.md"};function i(r,e,d,h,c,l){return a(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="one-workspace-and-the-graph" tabindex="-1">One workspace and the Graph <a class="header-anchor" href="#one-workspace-and-the-graph" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;One workspace and the Graph&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Updated 2026-10-28.</p><h2 id="question" tabindex="-1">Question <a class="header-anchor" href="#question" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Question&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After the drag pass the user said the Agent canvas and the workspace should be one page: the person and the Agent can share a context only if they work in the same place. They asked for a Graph page instead, as a way of showing what the Agent did, and gave four references: a project graph of questions, data, scripts, tables, figures and notes joined by labelled relations; a task panorama with stages, cards that carry tables and charts, an Agent flag on the card it works on and a timeline of small actions; a focus path through one result with a legend separating recorded relations from Agent suggestions; and a stage flow with a side panel. They left the treatment open (&quot;你觉得要做出彩，应该怎么做就怎么做&quot;).</p><p>The references set the kind of page, not values to copy. The questions:</p><ol><li>Do the person&#39;s views and the Agent&#39;s files land in one workspace either can arrange?</li><li>Can a person tell from one page what the Agent read, changed and ran for each question, and what came of it, without opening the conversation?</li><li>Can a person trace one result back to its data and question, and watch the work happen, live or replayed?</li></ol><h2 id="observed-before" tabindex="-1">Observed before <a class="header-anchor" href="#observed-before" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Observed before&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Following opened the Agent&#39;s files in a separate <code>agent-canvas</code> workspace. The person&#39;s own workspace (<code>workspace</code>, where Open in Studio and Files placed views) never received them, so the two had different views of the same files.</li><li>The Agent page listed each message&#39;s files and commands as text. Nothing joined a file one message wrote to the message that read it later.</li><li>The conversation record gives each tool step one time, its latest report: when it started while it runs and when it returned once it has. A finished command&#39;s record does not say when it started.</li><li>A folder walk listed names and sizes, not when a file changed, so nothing could say which files changed while a command ran.</li></ul><h2 id="changed" tabindex="-1">Changed <a class="header-anchor" href="#changed" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Changed&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Rho only:</p><ul><li><p><strong>One workspace</strong> (<code>web/canvas.ts</code>, <code>web/main.tsx</code>, <code>web/project.tsx</code>, <code>web/preview.tsx</code>, <code>web/overview.tsx</code>). Following, Open in Studio, opening a file from Files and a file named on the Agent page all use the workspace on screen, else the one last open in this tab, else the first, else a new <code>workspace</code>. A file the Agent opens joins the group the Agent&#39;s work made for its side, else a group already holding that side&#39;s views (editor for code; table and media for data and figures), else an empty workspace&#39;s one group; otherwise its side gets a group at that edge. Only groups the Agent&#39;s work made close their oldest views past six. The workspace&#39;s own Follow Agent and Step away buttons are hidden there; Studio&#39;s Follow is the one control. A file the person opens is held while following goes on; one following brings is only shown. An existing <code>agent-canvas</code> stays an ordinary workspace.</p></li><li><p><strong>When files changed</strong> (<code>src/server.ts</code>, <code>src/protocol.ts</code>): <code>project.entries</code> returns <code>modifiedAt</code> for each entry.</p></li><li><p><strong>What changed during a message</strong> (<code>src/conversations.ts</code>, <code>src/protocol.ts</code>): the service walks the project&#39;s files (time and size, without <code>.rho</code> and <code>.git</code>) when a message starts and again when it ends, and keeps the added, modified and removed ones on the message as <code>files</code>. At most 20000 files are compared and 200 changes kept, the rest counted; a walk stopped at its limit marks the record partial and calls nothing removed. It says what changed meanwhile, not what made the change.</p></li><li><p><strong>The work as a graph</strong> (<code>src/work-graph.ts</code>, DOM-free). Nodes are each question, each project file a message read, edited or wrote, each command, and each file that changed on disk during a message. Edges carry their basis:</p><ul><li>the Agent reported it: read, edited, wrote, ran;</li><li>named in a command: the script a command runs, or another file it names;</li><li>seen changing on disk: changed while a command ran (between the step before it and its return), or during the message when no command was running. A finished message uses its recorded changes; a running one, or a record from before them, uses each file&#39;s last change time, up to when the next message was sent.</li></ul><p>Messages are named by conversation and message, so two conversations&#39; first messages stay apart.</p><p>A file a message changed is its output, not its input; reading it only after it changed is looking at the output. Refused steps and paths outside the project are left out. At most 6 conversations × 8 messages and 160 nodes are drawn; past that the newest messages are kept whole and the page says how many it left out.</p></li><li><p><strong>The Graph page</strong> (<code>web/graph.tsx</code>, <code>web/graph.css</code>; the sidebar row after Studio):</p><ul><li>each message is one row read left to right, from what it took in to what changed while its command ran; a file an earlier row touched appears in a later row as a small reference that goes there; questions stand in one column;</li><li>cards show a table&#39;s first rows and size and a figure&#39;s pixels (at most 16 previews a page, two read at a time, figures up to 2 MB), and a question&#39;s card the start of the Agent&#39;s answer;</li><li>choosing a node shows the path it came by and what it fed, and the inspector shows the file in its own view, its history and its relations, with Open in workspace; arrow keys walk along the edges and within a column;</li><li>the timeline marks each message as a band and each action as a tick; dragging, the arrow keys or Play show the graph as it stood then, with a caption naming the action; long pauses between messages are cut;</li><li>while the Agent works, its card carries the Agent&#39;s flag, new cards arrive with a short mark and the line into the live card moves; Follow keeps it in view and the files still open in the shared workspace, without leaving the Graph;</li><li>a step that waits for the person&#39;s choice turns its flag amber, the header shows Needs your choice, and the inspector answers it with the Agent&#39;s own options;</li><li>pan by dragging or scrolling, zoom with pinch, ⌘/Ctrl-scroll, the buttons or +/−/0; far out a card is its name, drawn to be read; a map shows the rest when the graph does not fit.</li></ul></li></ul><h2 id="runs" tabindex="-1">Runs <a class="header-anchor" href="#runs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Runs&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Evidence: <code>work/graph-20261027/</code> (ignored by Git). <code>look.mjs</code> drives a controlled peer that runs the real Rscript in a disposable project; <code>agent.mjs</code> asks the person&#39;s own Claude Code.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>What was looked at</th><th>Observed</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>look.mjs</code> 1</td><td>Two messages, whole graph</td><td>Inputs were drawn right of the question that read them</td><td>Layers keep each edge&#39;s direction; sources sit just before their reader</td></tr><tr><td><code>look.mjs</code> 2</td><td>Edge labels</td><td>Every output said &quot;changed meanwhile&quot;: a finished step&#39;s time is its return</td><td>A command spans the step before it to its return; its card sits at the start</td></tr><tr><td><code>look.mjs</code> 3–4</td><td>Fit, 1440 px</td><td>One long chain; at fit no title could be read</td><td>One row per message with references; large names far out; a map; opening at 78%</td></tr><tr><td><code>look.mjs</code> 5</td><td>Labels, replay</td><td>Labels overlapped; the caption lower-cased the command</td><td>Wider gaps, two-line labels, the question→run line hidden when a file joins them</td></tr><tr><td>Claude Code 1</td><td>Real run from the Graph</td><td>Claude asked to run a command and waited 8 minutes; the card said Running</td><td>A waiting step turns amber, the header says so and the inspector answers it</td></tr><tr><td>Claude Code 2</td><td>Two messages (English, Chinese), Sonnet 5.5</td><td>5 and 3 choices answered on the Graph; 61 s and 37 s; 9 views in one workspace, no page errors. Message 2 reran <code>analysis.R</code>, so the figure message 1 made was drawn only as message 2&#39;s output</td><td>Each message keeps what changed on disk while it ran</td></tr><tr><td>acceptance</td><td>Back-to-back messages</td><td><code>plot.R</code>, written in message 2, was drawn as changed in message 1: its 2.5 s grace ran past the next send</td><td>Changes belong to a message until the next one is sent</td></tr><tr><td>acceptance</td><td>Open in workspace while following</td><td>The workspace opened on <code>airquality.csv</code>, not the table asked for</td><td>A file the person opens is held</td></tr><tr><td>Claude Code 3</td><td>The same two messages again</td><td>5 and 3 choices answered on the Graph; 76 s and 40 s; no page errors. The figure reads Changed 2× and its path reaches both commands that rewrote it. The inspector&#39;s history squeezed each message&#39;s name into a sliver beside a long command</td><td>The name goes on its own line under what happened (<code>inspect.mjs</code>)</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="checks" tabindex="-1">Checks <a class="header-anchor" href="#checks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Checks&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>test/work-graph.test.mjs</code> (6): edges and the window of a finished command; later messages, refused steps, paths outside the project, the live step and a waiting choice; a change after the next message was sent, and two conversations&#39; messages kept apart; recorded changes that survive a later rewrite; a layout that is deterministic, without overlaps and with sources before readers; rows, references and aligned questions.</li><li><code>test/acp-conversations.test.mjs</code>: a message records the files added and removed on disk while it ran; a comparison stopped at its limit says it is partial and calls nothing removed. <code>test/web-style.test.mjs</code> caught a stylesheet token (<code>--k</code>) read but not declared.</li><li>Ledger: Rho 212/212 (serial) and Plugins 92/92 (<a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/VERIFICATION.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ledger</a>).</li><li><code>npm run acceptance:graph</code> 8/8 (above); <code>acceptance:agent-canvas</code> 10/10, now checking one workspace with the Agent&#39;s data group beside the person&#39;s script and Graph in the sidebar; <code>frontend</code> 13/13, <code>agent-ui</code> 7/7, <code>continuity</code> 7/7, <code>sources</code> 7/7, <code>objects</code> 5/5, <code>actions</code> 6/6, shell, pages, person and plugin UI (9 checks).</li><li><code>build:service</code>, <code>build:web</code>, the web type check and <code>check:contracts</code> passed.</li><li>Documents: links and anchors of this page, Status, Frontend, the index and the canvas episode were checked and their rendered pages read.</li></ul><h2 id="limits" tabindex="-1">Limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Limits&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Edges come from the Agent&#39;s reports, command lines and file times. A change seen while a command ran says when, not that the command made it; a file changed by something else at that moment would be drawn the same way.</li><li>A file a message is still writing, or one in a record from before the change record, is placed by its last change: a later message that rewrites it moves it there. Earlier versions are not drawn, only that each message changed the file.</li><li>Commands the Agent runs outside the project, such as reading its own Skill files, are drawn like the project&#39;s; their titles show paths outside the project.</li><li>At the opening zoom the map can cover the lower-left card until the view moves.</li><li>Only files the folder walk reaches (48 folders, 5 levels, 4000 files) can be seen changing.</li><li>The Agent&#39;s own account of its work (<code>task.map.declare</code>, items with <code>from</code>) is not drawn yet; the Graph shows only what the records show.</li><li>Previews capture a snapshot of the file through Files, as showing it in place does.</li><li>No person other than the builder has used the page.</li></ul><h2 id="the-timeline-the-overview-and-host-activity" tabindex="-1">The timeline, the Overview and Host activity <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-timeline-the-overview-and-host-activity" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The timeline, the Overview and Host activity&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Updated 2026-10-28. The user called the Host activity section on Outside Rho &quot;still like shit&quot;, asked for the Overview too, and for the bar under the Graph to be richer, with two references: a panoramic timeline with a legend of kinds, coloured blocks, a time axis and a labelled current-time marker; and one swimlane per Agent with thinking, tool, waiting and failed blocks, play and 1×/2× speed.</p><p>Observed before, on a copy of the person&#39;s own project (two real conversations, five messages, six figures in <code>ggplot2-demo/out</code>), at 1440 and 390 px:</p><ul><li>The Graph&#39;s bar was one flat strip of equal dots. It could not say which conversation a step belonged to, what kind of step it was, or how long a pause was.</li><li>The Overview listed workspaces and results as text and carried the observation&#39;s diagnostics as paragraphs. None of the six figures was shown as a picture.</li><li>Host activity (the Agent plugin&#39;s <code>ActivityFeed</code>) was paragraphs under a heading: the lost Host, the counts, each action and the output folder all in the same text.</li></ul><p>Changed:</p><ul><li><strong>Timeline.</strong> One lane per conversation, named by its title and Agent mark. Each step is a block in its kind&#39;s colour, read from the same <code>GraphEvent</code> actions the Graph draws (asked, read, edited, ran, changed on disk, answered); a refused or unknown step is marked as failed. The legend counts each kind and filters to it. Messages less than 30 s apart form one stretch, sized by the square root of its length; between stretches the pause folds to a 44 px gap labelled with its length. The axis picks a tick step that keeps labels 72 px apart. Hovering a block names it and its time; replay labels the head with its time and plays at 1×, 2× or 4×.</li><li><strong>Overview.</strong> The same timeline in small (no controls) heads the page under &quot;What the Agent did&quot; and one line: questions, conversations, commands, files changed and the last time. Results follow as cards newest first, a figure as its pixels and a table as its first rows (<code>web/previews.ts</code>, shared with the Graph&#39;s cards), eight in all. Workspaces are cards naming their views. Shared notes is one row with its unsaved state; what the observation left out folds under Observation notes.</li><li><strong>Host activity</strong> (Rho-plugins, Agent 0.4.14). <code>ActivityFeed</code> draws itself with a prefixed stylesheet on the embedding&#39;s colour tokens: a lost Host is one card with Reconnect, counts are tiles, each action a card with its state, and Outputs a folder field and file rows. Its reads, limits and wording of facts are unchanged.</li></ul><p>Runs (<code>work/timeline-20261028/look.mjs</code>, evidence in <code>before/</code>, <code>after*/</code>):</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>Observed</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1440, Graph</td><td>Both lanes were titled &quot;hi&quot;, the first message</td><td>Lanes use the Agent&#39;s title for the conversation</td></tr><tr><td>1440, Graph</td><td>The pause label sat on the next stretch&#39;s first tick</td><td>The gap became 44 px and the label a small pill</td></tr><tr><td>390, Host</td><td>Rho&#39;s label style stacked &quot;Project folder&quot; over its field</td><td>The plugin&#39;s form row sets its own direction and margin</td></tr><tr><td>390, Host</td><td>&quot;Refresh outputs&quot; broke onto two lines</td><td>Buttons keep one line; the form wraps instead</td></tr><tr><td><code>acceptance:frontend</code>, four widths</td><td>The Overview card selector had changed. Registered run results showed only their kind under a hashed <code>.rho/plugins/runs/…</code> folder; on phones shared notes stood centred in a column</td><td>The check opens the workspace card; a result previews its exact version and reads Run output; the notes keep icon and text side by side</td></tr><tr><td>1440 and 390, all three</td><td>23 actions in two lanes with a 2.8 h fold; six figure thumbnails; the lost-Host card; no page errors, no horizontal overflow</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Checks: ledger Rho 218/218 and Plugins 92/92 (<a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho/blob/main/docs/VERIFICATION.json" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ledger</a>); <code>graph</code> 8/8, <code>frontend</code> 13/13, <code>continuity</code> 7/7, <code>agent-page</code> 7/7, <code>agent-canvas</code> 10/10, <code>agent-ui</code> 7/7, <code>sources</code> 7/7, <code>objects</code> 5/5, <code>actions</code> 6/6, <code>plugin-dx</code> 3/3, shell, pages at four widths, person and plugin UI; build, the web type check and <code>check:contracts</code> passed.</p><p>Limits:</p><ul><li>Block colours say what the record says a step was, not whether its result is right. Changed on disk keeps the Graph&#39;s limit: it says when, not who.</li><li>The Overview shows eight results. A file&#39;s preview captures a snapshot through Files and a registered result is read at its version; at most 16 per page, two at once, figures up to 2 MiB and tables to 3 rows by 4 columns. A file that cannot be previewed shows its kind.</li><li>The activity feed was then run with real Claude Code and dsh through the collector (<a href="/Rho/docs/concepts/agent-activity#real-episode-and-review">runs 7–8</a>): paths now read relative to the project and opening the section brings it into view.</li><li>No person other than the builder has used these pages.</li></ul>',30)])])}const w=t(n,[["render",i]]);export{g as __pageData,w as default};
